<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/constans-ii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constans-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-10">10 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Eugene I becomes pope after Constans II banishes Martin I</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Eugene I was chosen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> after Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constans-ii">Constans II</a> had Martin I arrested, carried off to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> and banished to Cherson for his strong opposition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monothelitism">Monothelitism</a>. Eugene held the office until his death on 2 June 657.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constans-ii">Constans II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monothelitism">Monothelitism</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
